			<view isee:template_view="template:11" isee:name="Static Insight 4" isee:original_design="Deluxe Prev-Next Blue Green Pastel" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" isee:scroll_x="56" type="interface">
				<style>
					<isee:stacked_container item_spacing="0" corner_radius="4" selected_item_color="black" selected_item_background="white" item_background="#DDDDDD" transparent_bg="false"/>
				</style>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_weight="bold" text_align="right" vertical_text_align="bottom" font_color="#284B63" font_size="28pt" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="52.1481" y="127.381" width="387.881" height="37.4271">CHP service split  results</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_color="#3D405B" font_size="14pt" padding="5" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="104.617" y="179.127" width="395.249" height="359.492">CHP services are split by age group. 
The majority of services are routine assessments by age group - with 15-64 year olds recorded as the largest group. 
Under fives and over 65s are assessed at each household visit; other groups on 1/3 of visits.

As the timeline moves towards 2040, the proportion spent on age 65 and over increases. 

In subcounties with malaria treatment, supply availability and CHP community treatment drives down the malaria prevalence and treatment need, leaving resource for other services.   
</text_box>
