			<view isee:template_view="template:11" isee:name="Static Insight 7" isee:original_design="Deluxe Prev-Next Blue Green Pastel" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" type="interface">
				<style>
					<isee:stacked_container item_spacing="0" corner_radius="4" selected_item_color="black" selected_item_background="white" item_background="#DDDDDD" transparent_bg="false"/>
				</style>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_weight="bold" text_align="right" vertical_text_align="bottom" font_color="#284B63" font_size="28pt" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="52.1481" y="117.381" width="387.881" height="44.6154">CHP dashboard results</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_color="#3D405B" font_size="14pt" padding="5" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="95.3867" y="181.515" width="395.249" height="364.876">Household visits - eCHIS peak in 2024 in all areas falling back in 2025 may reflect issues with eCHIS service interruption in 2025. Differing eCHIS implementation speed in different counties means that some counties show well below modelled results.  

eCHIS records show higher numbers of assessments and NCD screening services than seems reasonable in subcounties with established reporting. 

Modelled deworming services supplied by CHPs are greater than KHIS records, suggesting supplies may run at less than the 50% base case. 

Modelled diarrhoea treatment services are higher than KHIS records, suggesting potential under-reporting. 



</text_box>
