					</graph>
				</stacked_container>
				<text_box border_color="#00557F" border_width="2" border_style="solid" x="27.8846" y="98.592" width="146.154" height="431.501">These results show the effect of different malaria community case management (CCM) policies. 

Where CCM is implemented, malaria prevalence reduces, even with suboptimum supplies, due to timely detection and treatment.

The prevalence drops faster as supplies increase. 
 
Historical records imply under-reporting of malaria in the community. 

Overtreatment occurs when testing supplies are unavailable but treatment supplies are in stock.</text_box>
				<text_box x="321.769" y="106.923" width="62.3077" height="14.6438">POLICIES:</text_box>
