			<view isee:template_view="template:11" isee:name="Static Insight 8" isee:original_design="Deluxe Prev-Next Blue Green Pastel" background="white" page_width="1066" page_height="600" type="interface">
				<style>
					<isee:stacked_container item_spacing="0" corner_radius="4" selected_item_color="black" selected_item_background="white" item_background="#DDDDDD" transparent_bg="false"/>
				</style>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_weight="bold" text_align="right" vertical_text_align="bottom" font_color="#284B63" font_size="28pt" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="105.994" y="118.15" width="371.726" height="40">CHP malaria service results</text_box>
				<text_box z_index="7" background="#C9D2D8" font_color="#3D405B" font_size="14pt" padding="5" border_color="#3D405B" border_width="thick" vertical_scrollbar="true" appearance="transparent" x="101.54" y="173.742" width="395.249" height="390.261">Malaria management at community level is shown to drive down prevalence over time. In this model, poorer subcounties with greater reliance on CHPs benefit most, and prevalence reduces fastest, because a higher proportion of the population accesses CHP malaria test and treat services.

Historical comparison in Kakamega County suggests that where CCM is implemented, supplies have been available at about 75% of the ideal rate.

Stopping CCM shows a reversal of the reduction trend. 

Implementing CCM in other counties such as Turkana demonstrates prevalence reduction, starting about a year after the programme is implemented.

Note that this is an approximation of the impact of CHPs on malaria. Linkages to no-community malaria management and seasonality variations would be required for more accurate predictions. 
 

 </text_box>
				<stacked_container x="570.294" y="134.23" width="429.024" height="327.925" z_index="9" isee:appearance="tabs">
					<graph axis_label_font_size="16pt" width="429.024" height="327.925" comparative="true" type="time_series" show_grid="false" isee:tick_type="none" include_units_in_legend="false" isee:marker_type="letters" isee:label_pie_slices="false" isee:show_pie_borders="true" num_x_grid_lines="0" num_y_grid_lines="0" num_x_labels="5" num_y_labels="6" isee:page_title="Malaria prevalence" isee:fill_intensity="0.1" from="2020" x_axis_title="year" isee:allow_zero_axis="true" left_axis_title="Percentage" left_axis_multi_scale="false" left_axis_auto_scale="true" left_include_units="true" right_axis_multi_scale="false" right_axis_auto_scale="false" right_include_units="true">
						<plot isee:immediately_update_on_user_input="true" color="#00AA00" isee:keep_zero_visible="true" pen_width="2" index="0" show_y_axis="true">
							<entity name="mal.malaria_prevalence_compare[?]"/>
						</plot>
					</graph>
				</stacked_container>
			</view>
